[Joshua 12:7] And these are the sovereigns of the land which Yehoshua and the children of Yisra’ěl struck beyond the Yarděn, on the west, from Ba‛al Gaḏ in the Valley of Leḇanon as far as Mount Ḥalaq that goes up to Sě‛ir, which Yehoshua gave to the tribes of Yisra’ěl as a possession according to their divisions,
[12:8] in the mountain country, and in the low country, and in the desert plain, and in the slopes, and in the wilderness, and in the South, the Ḥittites, the Amorites and the Kena‛anites, the Perizzites, the Ḥivvites, and the Yeḇusites:
[12:9] the sovereign of Yeriḥo, one; the sovereign of Ai, which is beside Běyth Ěl, one;
[12:10] the sovereign of Yerushalayim, one; the sovereign of Ḥeḇron, one;
[12:11] the sovereign of Yarmuth, one; the sovereign of Laḵish, one;
[12:12] the sovereign of Eḡlon, one; the sovereign of Gezer, one;
[12:13] the sovereign of Deḇir, one; the sovereign of Geḏer, one;
[12:14] the sovereign of Ḥormah, one; the sovereign of Araḏ, one;

[Joshua 12:15] the sovereign of Liḇnah, one; the sovereign of Aḏullam, one;
[12:16] the sovereign of Maqqěḏah, one; the sovereign of Běyth Ěl, one;
[12:17] the sovereign of Tappuvaḥ, one; the sovereign of Ḥěpher, one;
[12:18] the sovereign of Aphěq, one; the sovereign of Sharon, one;
[12:19] the sovereign of Maḏon, one; the sovereign of Ḥatsor, one;
[12:20] the sovereign of Shimron Měron, one; the sovereign of Aḵshaph, one;
[12:21] the sovereign of Ta‛anaḵ, one; the sovereign of Meḡiddo, one;
[12:22] the sovereign of Qeḏesh, one; the sovereign of Yoqne‛am in Karmel, one;
[12:23] the sovereign of Dor in the heights of Dor, one; the sovereign of the nations of Gilgal, one;
[12:24] the sovereign of Tirtsah, one – thirty-one sovereigns in all.

[Joshua 13:8] With them the other half tribe the Re’uḇěnites and the Gaḏites received their inheritance, which Mosheh had given them, beyond the Yarděn eastward, as Mosheh the servant of <dn>YeHoVaH</dn> had given them:
[13:9] from Aro‛ěr which is on the bank of the wadi Arnon, and the city that is in the middle of the wadi, and all the plain of Měyḏeḇa as far as Diḇon;
[13:10] and all the cities of Siḥon sovereign of the Amorites, who reigned in Ḥeshbon, as far as the border of the children of Ammon;
[13:11] and <dn>את</dn> Gil‛aḏ, and the border of the Geshurites, and of the Ma‛aḵathites, and all Mount Ḥermon, and all Bashan as far as Salḵah;
[13:12] all the reign of Oḡ in Bashan, who reigned in Ashtaroth and Eḏre‛i, who remained of the remnant of the Repha’ites, for Mosheh had stricken and dispossessed them.
[13:13] However, the children of Yisra’ěl did not drive out <dn>את</dn> the Geshurites nor <dn>את</dn> the Ma‛aḵathites, so the Geshurites and the Ma‛aḵathites dwell in the midst of Yisra’ěl to this day.
[13:14] Only to the tribe of Lěvi he had given no inheritance – the offerings made by fire to <dn>YeHoVaH</dn> <dn>Elohim</dn> of Yisra’ěl were their inheritance, as <dn>He</dn> said to them.
